  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The gradient of a curve from first principles, the power rule for differentiation, and reversing it to integrate.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — The power rule",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}x^{n}=nx^{n-1} \\); the gradient at a point is the value of \\( \\tfrac{dy}{dx} \\) there. Integration reverses this: \\( \\displaystyle\\int x^{n}\\,dx=\\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C \\) for \\( n\\neq-1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The amber line is a secant from \\( x=1 \\) to \\( x=1+h \\) on \\( y=x^{2} \\). Shrink \\( h \\) and watch its slope approach the tangent gradient, \\( 2 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Secant → tangent",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "asDerivCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A secant line approaching the tangent on a parabola",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "asDerivDataBtn",
          "panelId": "asDerivDataPanel",
          "descId": "asDerivDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "asDerivDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on f(x) = x²",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "asDerivH",
            "label": {
              "en": "Gap <b>h =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0.1,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 2,
            "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "asDerivHV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Gap h",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "asDerivSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "secant gradient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "The secant gradient is \\( 2+h \\); as \\( h\\to0 \\) it tends to the tangent gradient \\( 2 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Differentiate",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( nx^{n-1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Gradient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "value of \\( \\tfrac{dy}{dx} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Integrate",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Definite",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( F(b)-F(a) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( y=x^{2}+3x \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=2x+3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{1} 2x\\,dx \\).</p>\\[ \\left[x^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1}=1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the equation of the normal to the curve \\(y=x^3-4x\\) at the point where \\(x=2\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y(2)=8-8=0\\). \\(y'=3x^2-4\\Rightarrow y'(2)=8\\). Normal gradient \\(=-\\tfrac{1}{8}\\). Equation: \\(y=-\\tfrac{1}{8}(x-2)\\Rightarrow8y+x=2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
